      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>scheduling.tolerations</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies tolerations to append to pods, excluding duplicates, running with this runtime class during admission. This combines the set of nodes tolerated by the pod and the runtime class.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>RuntimeClass</code> object:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <file-name>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>For example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f runtime-class.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the <code>RuntimeClass</code> object to your pod to ensure it is scheduled to the appropriate operating system variant:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: my-windows-pod\nspec:\n  runtimeClassName: windows2025\n# ..."} lang="yaml" />
